From 8e78b50f79c6977b1c5e59502aae66a1812b0264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 00:41:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/35] Background Task mode and lifecycle (Task tool)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds `background: true` to the built-in Task tool: spawns a subagent,
returns immediately with a `task_id`, buffers the result on the
session, and lets the parent pick it up via `read_task_result` on the
next turn. Cancelling the parent cascades to running background
children. New `GET /global/background-tasks` endpoint exposes the
buffer for cross-session inspection.

Includes the wake-up mechanism that lets the parent become aware of
a finished background task without user input. `SessionPrompt.continue_`
issues a minimal turn (one synthetic text part) when
`SessionBackground.complete` schedules a wake-up.

The synthetic wake-up message went through three iterations to reach
its final form. Recording the history because the dead ends are
non-obvious:

  1. Empty text — dropped by `MessageV2.toModelMessagesEffect`, which
     leaves the assistant message trailing. Claude rejected this as a
     prefill.
  2. Single dot "." — accepted by the API, but the model treated it
     as a no-op user message, ignored the system-reminder, and replied
     with generic continuation text instead of calling
     `read_task_result`.
  3. Explicit directive — "[Background task complete] Call
     read_task_result(task_id=...)" — the model reliably calls the
     tool. The synthetic flag still suppresses chat-UI render of the
     wake-up message.

Future iterations of synthetic-message flows should start from
the directive form.
